  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARM: Global Facility to Decarbonize Transport Multi-Donor Trust Fund Contribution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project supports the work of the World Bank to help Armenia reduce emissions in its transport sector and prepare for future investment in sustainable transport infrastructure. The contribution will allow the World Bank to carry out studies that examine different transport options, assess economic and climate risks, and identify practical steps needed to improve how goods and people move within Armenia and across its borders. These studies will build on earlier analytical work and will guide the design of future projects by estimating costs, setting priorities, and preparing the groundwork for competitive tenders. The project will also help identify policies that can make trade and transport more efficient, strengthen links with neighbouring countries, and contribute to long-term economic development. By enabling this preparatory work, the project helps Armenia move towards cleaner transport solutions and creates conditions that can attract future public and private investment.</narrative>
  </description>
